## 5. Development & Dogfooding Workflow

A core tenet of {{ PROJECT_NAME }} is **self-hosting / dogfooding**: using {{ PROJECT_NAME }} itself to continuously test and audit the {{ PROJECT_NAME }} web application during development.

### 5.1 Code Synchronization
Code is written on `{{ DEV_HOST }}` and synchronized to `{{ VM_NAME }}` for building and testing:

```bash
# Sync local codebase to the {{ PROJECT_NAME }} VM (from project root)
rsync -avz --exclude='.git' --exclude='node_modules' --exclude='venv' \
  --exclude='.env*.local' --exclude='dist' --exclude='.next' --exclude='__pycache__' \
  ./ {{ VM_NAME }}:{{ REMOTE_CODE_DIR }}
```

### 5.2 Executing {{ PROJECT_NAME }} Audits on Its Own Components
When a developer updates the {{ PROJECT_NAME }} Landing Page, Onboarding flow, or Customer Dashboard:
1. The web application is built and started inside `{{ VM_NAME }}`.
2. The {{ PROJECT_NAME }} Workhorse launches isolated evaluation containers for:
   * **Human Visitor**: Auditing the {{ PROJECT_NAME }} marketing landing page and registration form.
   * **Human Customer**: Logging into a mock {{ PROJECT_NAME }} dashboard and testing project creation.
   * **AI Agent Visitor**: Testing whether AI answer engines and search agents can interpret {{ PROJECT_NAME }}'s value proposition.
   * **AI Agent Customer**: Testing whether an external AI agent can interact programmatically with {{ PROJECT_NAME }}'s authenticated endpoints.
3. The resulting itemized reports and screenshots are generated on `{{ VM_NAME }}` and synced back to `{{ DEV_HOST }}` for review.

### 5.3 Accessing the Live Web Application on {{ HYPERVISOR_HOST_TITLE }} (Zero Host Processes on {{ DEV_HOST_TITLE }})
The unified application server runs inside `{{ VM_NAME }}` on port {{ APP_INTERNAL_PORT }}. To enable browser access from `{{ DEV_HOST }}` (or any device on the physical LAN) with **zero tasks or processes running on `{{ DEV_HOST }}`**, hypervisor `{{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }}` runs a persistent systemd socket forwarder (`systemd-socket-proxyd`):

* **Service Definition**: `{{ PROXY_SOCKET_SERVICE }}` on `{{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }}`.
* **Access URL**: **`http://{{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }}:{{ PROXY_EXTERNAL_PORT }}/`** (or `http://{{ HYPERVISOR_LAN_IP }}:{{ PROXY_EXTERNAL_PORT }}/`).
* **Traffic Routing**: Transparently forwards all incoming TCP traffic, HTTP methods, WebSockets, and sub-paths (`/*`) received on port `{{ PROXY_EXTERNAL_PORT }}` to port `{{ APP_INTERNAL_PORT }}` inside `{{ VM_NAME }}`.

