## 6. Hypervisor Management & Snapshot Operations

Hypervisor-level operations are managed on `{{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }}` using `virsh`:

### 6.1 VM Lifecycle Commands
```bash
# Check VM status
ssh {{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }} "sudo virsh list --all"

# Start the VM
ssh {{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }} "sudo virsh start {{ VM_NAME }}"

# Gracefully shut down the VM
ssh {{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }} "sudo virsh shutdown {{ VM_NAME }}"

# Force stop the VM (if hung)
ssh {{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }} "sudo virsh destroy {{ VM_NAME }}"
```

### 6.2 Snapshot & Instant Rollback
Snapshots allow the VM to be reset to a pristine baseline state if tests or experimental container builds produce filesystem clutter:

```bash
# Create a pristine baseline disk snapshot (UEFI domain)
ssh {{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }} "sudo virsh snapshot-create-as --domain {{ VM_NAME }} --name {{ SNAPSHOT_BASE_NAME }} --disk-only --description '{{ SNAPSHOT_BASE_DESC }}'"

# List available snapshots
ssh {{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }} "sudo virsh snapshot-list {{ VM_NAME }}"

# Revert to baseline snapshot (shut down domain before reverting disk snapshot if required)
ssh {{ HYPERVISOR_HOST }} "sudo virsh snapshot-revert {{ VM_NAME }} {{ SNAPSHOT_BASE_NAME }}"
```

